 ## Overview
-This method performs direct volume ray casting in a fragment shader, rendering a volume defined by 3D textures using a 1D transfer function and gradient-based diffuse shading [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods by explicitly computing surface normals from pre-stored gradient data to apply Lambertian lighting, rather than relying solely on density accumulation or geometry occlusion [S1, unofficial].
+This method performs direct volume ray casting by sampling a 3D texture storing pre-computed integer isovalue and gradient magnitude data, allowing the fragment shader to sample surface properties directly without numerical differentiation [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from standard raycasting by weighting the transfer function opacity with the gradient magnitude to enhance edges and surfaces, and by using a lookup-based approach for lighting and visibility selection [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Volumetric Raycasting](3462-volumetric-raycasting.md) by replacing on-the-fly gradient computation with pre-sampled gradient magnitudes and adding isovalue-based selection logic [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs and Outputs:**
-The method takes a fragment position in clip space as input and renders to `oColor` (vec4) and `oNormal` (vec3) outputs [S1, unofficial]. It requires several uniform textures and parameters:
-- `cubeFront` (sampler2D, binding 0): Stores the entry point of the ray into the volume [S1, unofficial].
-- `cubeBack` (sampler2D, binding 1): Stores the exit point of the ray from the volume [S1, unofficial].
-- `volume` (sampler3D, binding 2): The 3D density/scalar field texture [S1, unofficial].
-- `gradients` (sampler3D, binding 3): Pre-computed gradient data, encoded as a 2D vector per voxel [S1, unofficial].
-- `transferFunction` (sampler1D, binding 4): Maps scalar values to RGBA color and opacity [S1, unofficial].
-- `bakedNoise` (sampler2D, binding 5): 2D noise texture for jittering [S1, unofficial].
-- `ciModelMatrixInverseTranspose` (mat3): Model-view matrix inverse transpose for normal transformation [S1, unofficial].
-- `light` (struct): Contains `direction` (vec3), `ambient` (vec3), and `diffuse` (vec3) [S1, unofficial].
-- `threshold` (ivec2): Range of iso values (0-255) to render. Default is `(0, 255)` [S1, unofficial].
-- `stepSize` (vec3): Step size in each dimension [S1, unofficial].
-- `iterations` (int): Maximum number of ray marching steps [S1, unofficial].
-- `diffuseShading` (bool): Flag to enable/disable shading [S1, unofficial].
-- `stepScale` (float): Parameter for opacity correction [S1, unofficial].
